One typo in his message: `--ofline` should be `--offline`. Run:

```bash
source /data/start_conda.sh
conda create --name louis_env --clone chaoran_cv --offline
```

`--offline` skips the remote index check, which matters on a machine behind the proxy. Takes a few minutes and writes several GB.

Then:

```bash
conda activate louis_env
source /data/pri/Ascend/latest/ascend-toolkit/set_env.sh
export BISHENG_INSTALL_PATH=/data/ci_env/daily/pkg/ccec/bin
export PATH=/data/ci_env/daily/pkg/compiler/tools/bishengir/bin:$BISHENG_INSTALL_PATH:$PATH
export TRITON_PRINT_AUTOTUNING=1
export TRITON_DEBUG=1
export TRITON_ALWAYS_COMPILE=1
export TRITON_DISABLE_FFTS=1
```

Verify it took:

```bash
which python
which hivmc
which bishengir-compile
```

`hivmc` resolving is the thing that was missing on fremont.

Save the env setup so you don't retype it each session:

```bash
cat > /home/yaolu/env.sh << 'EOF'
source /data/start_conda.sh
conda activate louis_env
source /data/pri/Ascend/latest/ascend-toolkit/set_env.sh
export BISHENG_INSTALL_PATH=/data/ci_env/daily/pkg/ccec/bin
export PATH=/data/ci_env/daily/pkg/compiler/tools/bishengir/bin:$BISHENG_INSTALL_PATH:$PATH
export TRITON_PRINT_AUTOTUNING=1
export TRITON_DEBUG=1
export TRITON_ALWAYS_COMPILE=1
export TRITON_DISABLE_FFTS=1
EOF
```

Then `source /home/yaolu/env.sh` at the start of each session.

